<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=8&y=2003">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=7&y=2003">July-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=6&y=2003">June-2003</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=5&y=2003">May-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=4&y=2003">April-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=3&y=2003">March-2003</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><CENTER><font size=+2>July, 2003</font><BR></center><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>News of late</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Wednesday - July 16th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>We are now down to 25 members.  Probably 10 of those don't play but a few hours per month.  Even so, I've had more fun recently in EQ than I had in quite a while.  My stress level is much lower and there's much more time to lazy around for tickles.<BR>
<BR>
In the single grouping I've been doing, Veksar and a few other places have been explored.  Seems to be quite the zone, indeed.  I'm hoping that the new expansion, <a href="http://everquest.station.sony.com/lostdungeons/" target="_ldon">Lost Dungeons of Norrath</a>, will have many more zones like it or better.  It has a wonderful atmosphere and very interresting geography.  Not simply the flat plains or wall-agro dungeons you usually see.  Sure, there are a couple of wall-agro spots, but not many for the complexity.<BR>
We got several pieces of loot.  Some were actually upgrades and some will make fine twink gear hehe.  The gobbies at the entrance of the zone were low enough for a group of low 50's to kill but the zone gets progressively more difficult.  The middle of the zone houses 52-56ish mobs then quickly steps to 60 and 63rd level mobs after a drop-off.  Most mobs appear to be undead, which is nice for those with ITU or potions thereof.  If you can gather the group, I'd suggest exploring around Veksar.<BR>
<BR>
We also did a little diving around the updated Droga.  The theme here appears to be HP.  The mobs aren't dangerously packed-in like they were, but the map is the same.  Near the entrance, mobs seem to be easy enough.  Tons of HP, but 50 to 55th level or so.  One nice thing is that each mob appears to drop an average of 15plat and can barely hit as hard as Wuddar(giggle).  They don't drop the gems you'd see in Sebilis, but it makes for an easy /split at the end of the night.<BR>
It doesn't take long to find the 60th+ mobs.  Again, they have tons of HP, but scarcely hit for 200-250ish.  There are some annoying casters, but for the most part, this is an awesome non-pop zone.  The un-00ber group or non-standard could come out quite nicely here without the stress of mobs hitting for 500-700ish every pull.  The exp is worthy, but not godly, and there are some interresting trinkets to be found.<BR>
If you can't form the perfect group and want to kick around in a no-hassle area for decent exp and platz, Droga is for you. It's not nearly as interresting as Veksar was, imho, but it has its appeal.<BR>
<BR>
On a sepearte note; we've had plenty of members leave Legerdemain for various reasons.  One of them sent me a tell recently saying, <B><I>'btw, thanks for teaching me how to play for the sole purpose of fun. :)  i really appreciate it now.'</I></B>  I'm truely glad this person is going to stop chasing their tail as so many seem to do.  This person has finally realised that, yes, the tail is attached to their butt.  Of course, I can't take full credit for their renewed enjoyment of Everquest and all of the great opportunities for fun that it offers, but I'm glad to have helped open their eyes.  It's not always easy to realise that the fun is in the journey and that the journey doesn't always need a destination to be fun.</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR>



</font>
